{"data":{"content":"Describe your extension(s) here before implementing them.\n","line_count":2,"path":"extension.txt","sha256":"46d8aa87a36b5275259b43a6ce7d0b397b7d83db5c4896269c63452a78fa68ac"},"hash":"927a1a0f19e797979ca5e9dcf439a7b004855923887713f04d8e1f41f2b59d5e","kind":"doc.open","prev_hash":"97f05f6cfc459dc998e697f9ebb69a06fe6eca8fa5f5911516d51d574614c653","seq":282,"t":2685317,"wall":"2026-11-24T01:01:19.696Z"}
{"data":{"diff_size":2451,"new_content":"Extension: Color Turtle Kaleidoscope\n\nMy extension combines three things: a color system with curved shapes, turtle graphics, and symmetry transforms. Together they make it easy to write short programs that produce colorful, intricate animated patterns such as mandalas, flowers, and spirals.\n\n1. Colors and curved shapes.\nA new record Rgb(r, g, b) describes a color, with each channel from 0 to 255. The built-in hsl(hue, saturation, lightness) also produces an Rgb, with hue in degrees (0-359) and saturation and lightness as percentages (0-100), which makes rainbow effects simple. Three new shapes accept a color:\n  - ColorLine(start, end, color): a straight line in a chosen color.\n  - Arc(center, radius, from, to, color): part of a circle, from angle `from` to angle `to` in degrees. It is drawn in from the first angle toward the second.\n  - Curve(start, control1, control2, end, color): a smooth cubic Bezier curve.\nPlain Line shapes keep the app's automatic palette, so all existing programs look the same as before. Because the language only has integers, sin(degrees, scale) and cos(degrees, scale) return the rounded value of scale times the sine or cosine.\n\n2. Turtle graphics.\nInstead of computing coordinates, a program can steer a \"turtle\" that draws as it moves. turtle(x, y, heading) creates a turtle. forward(t, distance), turn(t, degrees), pen_up(t), pen_down(t), pen_color(t, color), pen_width(t, width), and circle(t, radius, degrees) each return an updated turtle, and turtle_paths(t) returns the List(Path) it has drawn. Each move is timed to start when the previous one ends and takes time proportional to its length, so the animation shows the turtle drawing in order. A turtle tracks its position with sub-unit precision internally, so long sequences of turns do not drift.\n\n3. Coloring and symmetry transforms on any list of paths.\n  - gradient(paths, from_color, to_color) recolors the paths so the colors blend smoothly from the first path to the last.\n  - rainbow(paths) gives the paths hues that cycle through the full spectrum.\n  - rotate(paths, degrees) rotates every path around the origin.\n  - kaleidoscope(paths, n) makes n copies rotated evenly around the origin, so they all draw at the same time like a kaleidoscope.\n  - mirror(paths) adds a left-right reflection of the paths.\n\nNew example programs (for instance a turtle \"mandala\" and a rainbow \"flower\") show these features in use, and the shape slider can control values such as the number of kaleidoscope copies.\n","new_content_size":2509,"new_hash":"a2a2b61da2f91886d1d3792cc76dd2f71bf3966fb765ce499d9030ab6d0bd130","old_hash":"46d8aa87a36b5275259b43a6ce7d0b397b7d83db5c4896269c63452a78fa68ac","operation":"modify","path":"extension.txt"},"hash":"f710fa0bb9da75bef03fd24e2f51f7ca53093aafa999da63a52737ff5c688e31","kind":"fs.external_change","prev_hash":"927a1a0f19e797979ca5e9dcf439a7b004855923887713f04d8e1f41f2b59d5e","seq":283,"t":2685512,"wall":"2026-11-24T01:01:19.891Z"}
{"data":{"content":"//// The drawing Path types produced by the evaluator and rendered by the\n//// animator.\n////\n//// The canvas maps a 1000-wide box centred on the origin onto its full size, and\n//// x, y, and thickness are all in those units.\n\n/// A point in world coordinates.\npub type Point {\n  Point(x: Float, y: Float)\n}\n\npub type Shape {\n  Line(start: Point, end: Point)\n}\n\npub type Path {\n  // start and end are the times (in tenths of a second) between which the path is\n  // drawn: the reveal runs linearly from nothing at start to the complete shape at\n  // end. A path with end <= start appears complete the moment it starts.\n  Path(shape: Shape, start: Float, end: Float, thickness: Float)\n}\n","line_count":22,"path":"src\\shape.gleam","sha256":"de7813ac593728b2f322b3eecafb888bf088b35843b28b5b2b0d18b614de384e"},"hash":"28a174e5e68ea74bdc317845d286744e414d1b3c33b5f93a8456b358331e80cc","kind":"doc.open","prev_hash":"f710fa0bb9da75bef03fd24e2f51f7ca53093aafa999da63a52737ff5c688e31","seq":284,"t":2690662,"wall":"2026-11-24T01:01:25.041Z"}
